@cc [owner:Nils-Fedrigo,label:product] replacement-model-preserves-reasoning-effort
A model config introduced to replace another must expose the same `supportedReasoningEfforts`,
`defaultReasoningEffort` and `configParsers` as the model it replaces, or ship a migration
rewriting `agent_configurations.reasoningEffort` for the agents it takes over: repointing
`agent_configurations.modelId` alone must never change the effort an existing agent runs at.

@cc [owner:pmilliotte,label:product] effort-sent-as-selected
A Dust endpoint must send the provider the reasoning effort it was given: `configParsers` must not
rewrite `reasoning.effort`. Two exceptions: `disableReasoningWhenForcingTool` turns reasoning off when
the provider rejects a forced tool call with thinking on, and `dropReasoning` omits the field for
models whose only supported effort is `none`. An effort the provider does not accept is
marked unsupported in the model's `supportedReasoningEfforts` instead of being remapped to another.
